{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1789166197,"nonce":"DQBZH7wHIQ1m8jhjV6Q6LucX6MY=","message":"Fixed in 1bee177. results.json carries run_id/run_url of the sweep that measured it (from the aggregate job's GITHUB_RUN_ID), and the page's provenance line reads 'measured \u003cdate\u003e · sweep #\u003cid\u003e' with a link, so a republish shows the same sweep id and date as the deploy that first published it.\n\nAlso found while fixing: the republish selected the newest PUSH-triggered sweep, and since 41ded9c sweeps run only by schedule or dispatch, so every conformance-triggered deploy reverted the site to run 34387507221 (2026-09-09). Each daily sweep then restored fresh numbers until the next push. Now it takes the newest successful run whose event is not workflow_run.","files":null}]}